# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  apps/admin — Vercel project "apna-ghar-admin"  (Root Directory: apps/admin)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  TEMPLATE — committed. Copy to .env. `pnpm --filter @ghar/admin dev` serves :3001.
#  Vercel bakes env vars in at BUILD time — redeploy after changing one.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ⚠️ THE TRAP: admin and share both read a variable called API_BASE_URL and
# expect DIFFERENT values. Admin appends paths like /admin/agents/…, so it
# needs the /api suffix. Share fetches /s/:token, which main.ts excludes from
# the global prefix, so it must NOT have it. Get this backwards and you get
# 404s that look like auth failures.
#
#   local     http://localhost:3000/api
#   deployed  https://apna-ghar-api.vercel.app/api
API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000/api

# Public base of the R2 bucket — the payments queue renders manual-payment
# proof screenshots from it. Blank just means broken images on that one page;
# it is the same value as the API's R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL.
MEDIA_BASE_URL=

# Sign in with the seeded admin: 0300 9999999, code 123456
# (works while the API has OTP_DEV_MODE=true).
